00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:57,428
Deepsea Challenger (DCV 1) is a 7.3-metre (24 ft) deep-diving submersible designed to
reach the bottom of the Challenger Deep, the deepest-known point on Earth.

10
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
On 26 March 2012, Canadian film director James Cameron piloted the craft to
accomplish this goal in the second crewed dive reaching the Challenger Deep.

11
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
Built in Sydney, Australia, by the research and design company Acheron Project Pty Ltd, Deepsea Challenger includes scientific sampling equipment
and high-definition 3-D cameras; it reached the ocean's deepest point after two hours and 36 minutes of descent from the surface.

